# An `X "c"` hint that decides no shift/reduce conflict is rejected: the
# LR(1) lookaheads already separate the cases, so the hint has no effect.
# error: dead_x_hint.grammar:20:
# error: X ":" on name
# error: has no effect
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    colon
    eof
    err
':'                                         → colon
[a-zA-Z]+                                   → ident
.                                           → err
@parser
# (no @conflicts block: the grammar must be conflict-free)
program! = entry ":" IDENT                  → (entry 1 3)
         | entry                            → (entry 1)
entry    = name                             → 1
name     = IDENT X ":"                      → 1
